5:["$","article",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 prose prose-slate","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"Microbial Consortia Bioenergy: A PRISM-9 Walkthrough"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-xs text-slate-500 not-prose","children":"2026-05-24"}],"$Ld"]}]
d:[["$","blockquote",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Note:"}]," This walkthrough is ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"illustrative"}],". Specific graph sizes, factor selections, and proposal numbers reflect a representative scenario for the methodology, not a peer-reviewed clinical trial result. Where we cite figures from a production run, they are clearly labeled as such."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"When we picked the first vertical slice for FastScience! v7, we deliberately chose a problem with three properties: large literature, real economic stakes, and working researchers willing to validate every claim."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["We landed on ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"microbial consortia bioenergy"}]," — specifically, two-organism consortia for methane yield from agricultural digestate."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"The problem"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Anaerobic digestion of corn-stover slurry produces methane. Reported yields vary several-fold across published studies, and no single factor fully explains the variance. Single-organism cultures tend to underperform; two-organism consortia sometimes win dramatically and sometimes collapse."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Hypothesis: there is a small set of dominant variables — substrate composition, dominant species pair, retention time, micronutrient availability, pH buffering — that explain most of the variance."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"What the graph looks like (representative production figures)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"After ingesting the relevant literature (drawn from public sources including PubMed and AGRICOLA), our Neo4j graph for this domain currently holds approximately:"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"~14,000 entities"}]," — organisms, substrates, intermediates, environmental conditions, observed outcomes."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"~50,000 typed arcs"}]," — ",["$","code",null,{"children":"metabolizes"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"inhibits"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"co-occurs-with"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"produces"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"~200 distinct outcome metrics"}]," — methane yield, VFA accumulation, biomass production, etc."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"These figures are from one snapshot of the production graph at the time of writing and will grow as new literature is ingested."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"What PRISM-9 picks for this question"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["For the question ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"maximize methane yield from corn-stover digestate,\""}]," PRISM-9 reduces that graph to these 9 dominant factors:"]}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Dominant primary degrader genus (e.g. ",["$","em",null,{"children":"Clostridium"}]," vs ",["$","em",null,{"children":"Ruminococcus"}],")"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Secondary methanogen species (e.g. ",["$","em",null,{"children":"Methanosarcina"}]," vs ",["$","em",null,{"children":"Methanosaeta"}],")"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"C:N ratio of input substrate"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Hydraulic retention time"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Operating pH (buffered vs unbuffered)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Trace-element supplementation (Ni / Co availability)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Inoculum source (e.g. cow rumen vs municipal digester sludge)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Temperature regime (mesophilic vs thermophilic)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Pre-treatment of substrate (none vs steam-explosion vs alkaline)"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Notably absent for this specific question: total VFA load, ammonia concentration, mixing rate. PRISM-9 deemed these correlated-but-not-causal at the reduction threshold."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"What Cube-27 surfaces"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"The 9 factors fan out into 27 leaf variables. The QUBO solver returns one strongly causally coherent candidate configuration of the form:"}],"\n",["$","blockquote",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Ruminococcus albus"}]," + ",["$","em",null,{"children":"Methanosarcina barkeri"}],", mesophilic, C:N ≈ 25, retention ≈ 18d, buffered to pH ≈ 7.0, Ni-supplemented, rumen inoculum, steam-exploded substrate."]}],"*"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Other near-optimal configurations are returned as alternatives; users review them before booking experiments."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"The kind of experiment that gets proposed"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"From a configuration like the above, the ARS engine emits a comparative trial outline — typically the favored configuration plus one or two single-variable perturbations plus an industry-standard control. The output includes order-of-magnitude cost and timing estimates and a shortlist of registered CROs capable of executing the protocol."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"End-to-end time from a freeform research question to a ranked experiment proposal in a Researcher-tier session is on the order of an hour or two, depending on domain manual readiness and human sign-off pace."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"What this is and is not"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["This is a methodology walkthrough — a demonstration of how the FastScience! v7 pipeline behaves on a non-trivial bioenergy question. It is ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"not"}]," a peer-reviewed claim about specific microbial consortia performance. Treat the proposed configurations as hypotheses requiring experimental verification, exactly as you would treat any other computationally generated hypothesis."]}]]
